fice Supplies 22.75\n12 2026-03-18 Figma seats Software 90\n13 2026-03-18 Client dinner Meals 318.6\n14 2026-03-20 Desk lamp Furniture 64\n15 2026-03-22 Hotel (2 nights) Travel 412\n16 2026-03-24 USB-C cables Equipment 31.96\n17 2026-03-25 Team lunch Meals 212.4\n18 2026-03-27 Pens Office Supplies 9.8\n19 2026-03-30 Taxi to airport Travel 58\n20 2026-03-31 Notion subscription Software 96\n\nAll good.\n\nDate column serial values. Could set `t=\"n\"`? Not necessary for numeric. For inline strings, no xml:space? `<t xml:space=\"preserve\">` if leading/trailing none. Fine.\n\nNeed summary maybe include year. Let's calculate average, largest. $3,542.60/18 = 196.8111 -> 196.81. Largest 1240. Fine.\n\nCould include \"Net total\" no.\n\nNeed maybe use conditional formatting? unnecessary.\n\nNeed column widths. Summary:\nA 24, B 16, C 22, D 18. With KPI labels A/C, values B/D. But section table columns A-D reuse widths. Category A 24, transactions B 16, total C 22, share D 18. That works.\nRow heights.\n\nNeed style for merged header section row. If merged across A:D and style 12 with fill. Fine.\n\nPotential xlsx compatibility issue: Merged cells with styles across all, but only top-left value. That's okay. We set each cell? For merged A1:D1, only A1 value. B1 etc absent. Fine.\n\nPotential issue cell style fill uses RGB 8 hex. Good.\n\nNeed perhaps include `xmlns:mc` and `mc:Ignorable`? Not necessary.\n\nNeed perhaps workbook relationships include theme if no theme? Omit. Excel may automatically default. Fine.\n\nNeed perhaps styles require `<numFmts>` before `<fonts>` yes per schema order: numFmts, fonts, fills, borders, cellStyleXfs, cellXfs, cellStyles, dxfs, tableStyles. Good.\n`<xf ... applyNumberFormat=\"1\">`.\nNeed `xfId=\"0\"` for cellXfs? In cellXfs each xf attributes: numFmtId, fontId, fillId, borderId, xfId. Add xfId=\"0\". Good.\nAlignment for default:\n```\n<alignment vertical=\"center\"/>\n```\nNeed quote.\n\nBorders:\n0 none\n1 bottom thin D9E2E2\n2 top thin? plus bottom medium? Use top and bottom.\nDefine:\n```\n<border><left/><right/><top style=\"thin\"><color rgb=\"FFB8CBCB\"/></top><bottom style=\"thin\"><color rgb=\"FFB8CBCB\"/></bottom><diagonal/></border>\n```\nMaybe border index 1 all thin light. index 2 top+bottom medium. Good.\n\nFills:\n0 none\n1 gray125\n2 0F4C5C\n3 E9F2F3\n4 F7FBFB\n5 D8E7E9\n6 FFFFFF maybe.\n\nFonts:\n0 11 #1F2937\n1 11 bold #FFFFFF\n2 18 bold #FFFFFF\n3 11 bold #0F4C5C\n4 10 italic #5B6B6B\n5 24 bold #0F4C5C\n6 9 #5B6B6B\n7 10 #5B6B6B\nMaybe font 7 for notes? note style 15 font 7. Fine.\n\nStyle details:\n1 header: font1 fill2 border1, center, wrap\n2 body: font0 fill0 border1, left center\n3 date: font0 fill0 border1, center, numFmt164\n4 currency: font0 fill0 border1, right\n5 alt body: font0 fill4 border1\n6 alt date: font0 fill4 border1\n7 alt currency: font0 fill4 border1\n8 title: font2 fill2, left center\n9 subtitle: font4, left center\n10 label: font3 fill3 border1 left center\n11 total currency: font3 fill3 border2, right, numFmt165\n12 section: font1 fill2 border1, left center\n13 KPI integer: font5 fill3 border1, center center, numFmt0\n14 KPI currency: font5 fill3 border1, center center, numFmt165\n15 note: font7 fill0, wrap, top left\n16 total label: font3 fill3 border2, left center\n17 body text right? unused maybe. Could use KPI text:\n17 KPI text: font3 fill3 border1, center center\n18 maybe total count: font3 fill3 border2, center center\n19 pct normal: font0 fill0 border1, center, numFmt166\n20 pct alt: font0 fill4 border1, center, numFmt166\n21 total pct: font3 fill3 border2, center, numFmt166\n22 blank? Hmm.\n\nNeed cellXfs count 22 maybe indexes 0-21. Good.\n\nSummary title row A1 style 8. Subtitle row A2 style 9. KPI labels style 10. Values.\nCategory header row 10 style 1.\nCategory details body styles 2/5, count style maybe center? normal text style 2 left. Better center count. Create style 22 body center: font0 fill0 border1 center. style 23 alt body center. Then rows:\nA cat style 2/5, B count style 22/23, C amount style 4/7, D pct style 19/20.\nTotal row B style 18; D style 21.\n\nAdd 22/23. So cellXfs count 24 indexes 0-23.\nLet's list:\n0 default\n1 header\n2 body\n3 date\n4 currency\n5 alt body\n6 alt date\n7 alt currency\n8 title\n9 subtitle\n10 label\n11 total currency\n12 section\n13 KPI integer\n14 KPI currency\n15 note\n16 total label\n17 KPI text\n18 total integer\n19 pct\n20 alt pct\n21 total pct\n22 body center\n23 alt body center\n\nGood.\n\nNeed cellStyleXfs count 1. `cellStyles` one.\n\n`numFmts`:\n164 date `yyyy\\-mm\\-dd`? Excel custom format code requires escaped hyphen? Hyphen is literal. `yyyy-mm-dd` works? Excel can interpret `m` as month and `d` day, hyphen separators. Standard. Fine.\n165 `$#,##0.00`\n166 `0.00%` maybe `0.0%`; use `0.0%` to 36.8%. The user may want more precision but okay. Use `0.0%`.\n\nCould use amount `$#,##0.00` which displays negative as -$? not relevant.\n\nNeed row 17 total. Calculate percentages maybe: 36.8, 2.3, 21.8, 9.5, 19.5, 10.2; sum 100.1 due rounding. Accept. Maybe one decimal shares. Could show 36.8%, 2.3%, 21.8%, 9.5%, 19.5%, 10.2%. Total 100.0? 36.8+2.3=39.1; +21.8=60.9; +9.5=70.4; +19.5=89.9; +10.2=100.1. Hmm sum with one decimal not exactly 100.0. Total row 100.0%. Fine. Could use two decimals: 36.81+2.29+21.78+9.46+19.48+10.19 = 100.01. Also rounding. Common. Could avoid total pct row or show \"100%\". Fine. Use 0.0%, total 100.0%. Slight 100.1 visible? Actually if individual rounded, display 100.1; total actual 1.0 displays 100.0. That's normal. Could format 0.00% to show 36.81 etc, total 100.00. Sum displays 100.01 maybe. Not perfect. Maybe percent values as text 37%, 2%, 22%, 9%, 19%, 10% sum 99. Hmm. Not crucial. Perhaps omit percentage column to keep summary simple and avoid rounding complaints. Instead category table columns: Category | Transactions | Total | Avg. \"Avg\" 652.00, 27.02, 192.85, 111.67, 172.55, 180.48. That's perhaps more useful. But total row average 196.81. We can do:\nA Category\nB Transactions\nC Total\nD Average\nRows. Total row: 18, 3542.60, 196.81.\nThis avoids share. Nice. Summary includes total spend and average anyway. But category breakdown with avg adds value. Let's do 4 columns Category | Transactions | Total spend | Avg.\nStyle normal amount and alt. D amount style same. Total row amount. Fine. No percent numFmt needed, simplify styles. But percentages are nice. May","truncated":true}
{"type":"tool_call","callId":"call_00_LlcY68tD3xFSDK2iTcdX0056","tool":"write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/vellery-bv5u6dxz/work/build_clean_expenses.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Build a cleaned March 2026 expense workbook without external dependencies.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport zipfile\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom datetime import date, datetime, timezone\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom xml.sax.saxutils import escape\n\nWORKDIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nXLSX_PATH = WORKDIR / \"cleaned_expenses.xlsx\"\nCSV_PATH = WORKDIR / \"cleaned_expenses.csv\"\n\n# Date, Description, Category, Amount. Duplicates from the source were removed,\n# dates resolved to March 2026, categories normalized, and amounts made numeric.\nTRANSACTIONS = [\n    (date(2026, 3, 2), \"Office chairs\", \"Furniture\", 1240.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 4), \"Printer paper\", \"Office Supplies\", 48.50),\n    (date(2026, 3, 5), \"Team lunch\", \"Meals\", 212.40),\n    (date(2026, 3, 9), \"Zoom subscription\", \"Software\", 149.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 10), \"Taxi to client\", \"Travel\", 36.20),\n    (date(2026, 3, 10), \"Train tickets\", \"Travel\", 184.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 12), \"Coffee beans\", \"Meals\", 27.99),\n    (date(2026, 3, 13), \"Monitor\", \"Equipment\", 329.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 15), \"Notebooks\", \"Office Supplies\", 22.75),\n    (date(2026, 3, 18), \"Figma seats\", \"Software\", 90.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 18), \"Client dinner\", \"Meals\", 318.60),\n    (date(2026, 3, 20), \"Desk lamp\", \"Furniture\", 64.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 22), \"Hotel (2 nights)\", \"Travel\", 412.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 24), \"USB-C cables\", \"Equipment\", 31.96),\n    (date(2026, 3, 25), \"Team lunch\", \"Meals\", 212.40),\n    (date(2026, 3, 27), \"Pens\", \"Office Supplies\", 9.80),\n    (date(2026, 3, 30), \"Taxi to airport\", \"Travel\", 58.00),\n    (date(2026, 3, 31), \"Notion subscription\", \"Software\", 96.00),\n]\n\nCATEGORY_ORDER = [\"Furniture\", \"Office Supplies\", \"Meals\", \"Software\", \"Travel\", \"Equipment\"]\nTOTAL = round(sum(t[3] for t in TRANSACTIONS), 2)\nCOUNT = len(TRANSACTIONS)\nAVERAGE = round(TOTAL / COUNT, 2)\nLARGEST = max(t[3] for t in TRANSACTIONS)\n\n\ndef excel_serial(d: date) -> int:\n    return (d - date(1899, 12, 30)).days\n\n\ndef money(value: float) -> str:\n    return f\"{value:.2f}\"\n\n\ndef inline_cell(ref: str, value: str, style: int) -> str:\n    return (\n        f'<c r=\"{ref}\" s=\"{style}\" t=\"inlineStr\">'\n        f'<is><t xml:space=\"preserve\">{escape(value)}</t></is></c>'\n    )\n\n\ndef number_cell(ref: str, value: float | int, style: int) -> str:\n    if isinstance(value, float):\n        rendered = repr(round(value, 2))\n    else:\n        rendered = str(value)\n    return f'<c r=\"{ref}\" s=\"{style}\"><v>{rendered}</v></c>'\n\n\ndef date_cell(ref: str, value: date, style: int) -> str:\n    return f'<c r=\"{ref}\" s=\"{style}\"><v>{excel_serial(value)}</v></c>'\n\n\ndef build_transactions_sheet() -> str:\n    rows: list[str] = []\n    rows.append(\n        '<row r=\"1\" ht=\"28\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n        + inline_cell(\"A1\", \"Date\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"B1\", \"Description\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"C1\", \"Category\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"D1\", \"Amount\", 1)\n        + \"</row>\"\n    )\n\n    for idx, (txn_date, description, category, amount) in enumerate(TRANSACTIONS, start=2):\n        alt = idx % 2 == 1\n        text_style = 5 if alt else 2\n        date_style = 6 if alt else 3\n        money_style = 7 if alt else 4\n        rows.append(\n            f'<row r=\"{idx}\" ht=\"22\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n            + date_cell(f\"A{idx}\", txn_date, date_style)\n            + inline_cell(f\"B{idx}\", description, text_style)\n            + inline_cell(f\"C{idx}\", category, text_style)\n            + number_cell(f\"D{idx}\", amount, money_style)\n            + \"</row>\"\n        )\n\n    last_row = COUNT + 1\n    return f'''<?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?>\n<worksheet xmlns=\"http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/spreadsheetml/2006/main\">\n  <dimension ref=\"A1:D{last_row}\"/>\n  <sheetViews>\n    <sheetView tabSelected=\"1\" workbookViewId=\"0\">\n      <pane ySplit=\"1\" topLeftCell=\"A2\" activePane=\"bottomLeft\" state=\"frozen\"/>\n      <selection pane=\"bottomLeft\" activeCell=\"A2\" sqref=\"A2\"/>\n    </sheetView>\n  </sheetViews>\n  <sheetFormatPr defaultRowHeight=\"15\"/>\n  <cols>\n    <col min=\"1\" max=\"1\" width=\"14\" customWidth=\"1\"/>\n    <col min=\"2\" max=\"2\" width=\"30\" customWidth=\"1\"/>\n    <col min=\"3\" max=\"3\" width=\"22\" customWidth=\"1\"/>\n    <col min=\"4\" max=\"4\" width=\"16\" customWidth=\"1\"/>\n  </cols>\n  <sheetData>\n    {''.join(rows)}\n  </sheetData>\n  <autoFilter ref=\"A1:D{last_row}\"/>\n  <pageMargins left=\"0.5\" right=\"0.5\" top=\"0.6\" bottom=\"0.6\" header=\"0.3\" footer=\"0.3\"/>\n  <pageSetup orientation=\"landscape\" fitToWidth=\"1\" fitToHeight=\"0\"/>\n</worksheet>'''\n\n\ndef build_summary_sheet() -> str:\n    category_totals = Counter()\n    category_counts = Counter()\n    for _, _, category, amount in TRANSACTIONS:\n        category_totals[category] += amount\n        category_counts[category] += 1\n\n    rows: list[str] = []\n    rows.append('<row r=\"1\" ht=\"40\" customHeight=\"1\">' + inline_cell(\"A1\", \"March 2026 Expense Report\", 8) + \"</row>\")\n    rows.append(\n        '<row r=\"2\" ht=\"24\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n        + inline_cell(\"A2\", f\"Cleaned transactions  ·  {COUNT} records  ·  ${TOTAL:,.2f} total\", 9)\n        + \"</row>\"\n    )\n    rows.append('<row r=\"3\" ht=\"10\" customHeight=\"1\"/>')\n\n    # KPI cards: label/value pairs in two columns.\n    kpi_rows = [\n        (4, \"Transactions\", COUNT, 13, \"Period\", \"Mar 2–31, 2026\", 17),\n        (5, \"Total spend\", TOTAL, 14, \"Categories\", len(category_totals), 17),\n        (6, \"Average transaction\", AVERAGE, 14, \"Duplicates removed\", 2, 17),\n        (7, \"Largest expense\", LARGEST, 14, \"Source rows\", 20, 17),\n    ]\n    for r, label1, val1, val_style1, label2, val2, val_style2 in kpi_rows:\n        rows.append(\n            f'<row r=\"{r}\" ht=\"26\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n            + inline_cell(f\"A{r}\", label1, 10)\n            + number_cell(f\"B{r}\", val1, val_style1)\n            + inline_cell(f\"C{r}\", label2, 10)\n            + (\n                number_cell(f\"D{r}\", val2, val_style2)\n                if isinstance(val2, (int, float))\n                else inline_cell(f\"D{r}\", val2, val_style2)\n            )\n            + \"</row>\"\n        )\n\n    rows.append('<row r=\"8\" ht=\"12\" customHeight=\"1\"/>')\n    rows.append('<row r=\"9\" ht=\"28\" customHeight=\"1\">' + inline_cell(\"A9\", \"Spending by category\", 12) + \"</row>\")\n    rows.append(\n        '<row r=\"10\" ht=\"24\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n        + inline_cell(\"A10\", \"Category\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"B10\", \"Transactions\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"C10\", \"Total spend\", 1)\n        + inline_cell(\"D10\", \"Share\", 1)\n        + \"</row>\"\n    )\n\n    start_row = 11\n    for offset, category in enumerate(CATEGORY_ORDER):\n        r = start_row + offset\n        alt = r % 2 == 0\n        text_style = 5 if alt else 2\n        count_style = 23 if alt else 22\n        money_style = 7 if alt else 4\n        pct_style = 20 if alt else 19\n        rows.append(\n            f'<row r=\"{r}\" ht=\"22\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n            + inline_cell(f\"A{r}\", category, text_style)\n            + number_cell(f\"B{r}\", category_counts[category], count_style)\n            + number_cell(f\"C{r}\", round(category_totals[category], 2), money_style)\n            + number_cell(f\"D{r}\", category_totals[category] / TOTAL, pct_style)\n            + \"</row>\"\n        )\n\n    total_row = start_row + len(CATEGORY_ORDER)\n    rows.append(\n        f'<row r=\"{total_row}\" ht=\"24\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n        + inline_cell(f\"A{total_row}\", \"Total\", 16)\n        + number_cell(f\"B{total_row}\", COUNT, 18)\n        + number_cell(f\"C{total_row}\", TOTAL, 11)\n        + number_cell(f\"D{total_row}\", 1.0, 21)\n        + \"</row>\"\n    )\n\n    notes_start = total_row + 2\n    rows.append(\n        f'<row r=\"{notes_start}\" ht=\"28\" customHeight=\"1\">'\n        + inline_cell(f\"A{notes_start}\", \"Cleaning notes\", 12)\n        + \"</row>\"\n    )\n    notes = [\n        \"Removed 2 exact duplicates: Office chairs ($1,240.00, Mar 2) and Printer paper ($48.50, Mar 4).\",\n        \"Resolved mixed date formats row by row and normalized every date to yyyy-mm-dd; all entries fall in March 2026.\",\n        \"Standardized categories to six values and converted all amounts to numeric currency.\",\n        \"Kept both $212.40 Team lunch entries because they occur on different dates (Mar "},"truncated":true}
